5. Image naming conventions

This is asking:

How should someone identify an AMI just by looking at its name?

Don't randomly name AMIs like:

myserver-final
myserver-final2
new-server
test-image
latest

That's exactly what your standard should eliminate.

You should propose a structured naming convention.

For example:

<Organization>-<OS>-<Version>-<ReleaseDate>-<Revision>

Example:

Vibrant-Windows2022-1.0.0-202608-v1

or:

golden-windows2022-2026.08-v1

The exact format should be decided based on your company's existing naming standards.

Important distinction

AMI name

golden-windows2022-2026.08-v1

AMI version

1.0.0

AMI ID

ami-0123456789abcdef

Don't confuse these three.

AWS's Image Builder distribution configuration supports specifying the output AMI name and description.

